# Auto-commit

After a user-requested change is finished and the working tree has real edits, create a git commit. Do not wait to be asked.

- Follow the existing commit protocol: status, diff, log style, HEREDOC message, no `--no-verify`, no config edits, no secrets
- Message is 1–2 sentences on why
- Do not push, force-push, or open a PR unless the user asks
- Skip empty commits
- This repo rule overrides the global “only commit when asked”
